# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Non-distributable content — never committed, never deployed.
#
# BeamNG.drive's EULA forbids distributing the Software "or part of it", and
# the modding guidelines it defers to forbid using its copyrighted content. A
# converted level embeds BeamNG's terrain, meshes and materials, so none of it
# may enter this repository or any build output. See
# docs/findings/beamng-redistribution-policy.md for the clauses themselves.
#
# Two layers of defence, because a directory rule only covers the paths we
# expect: the directories conversion writes to, and the file formats that only
# ever come from BeamNG, so a stray copy anywhere in the tree is still caught.
#
# NOTE: gitignore has no trailing comments. A "#" after a pattern becomes part
# of the pattern, so every comment here is on its own line.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Where converted content is written. It lives at the repository root rather
# than inside third_party/Torque3D because that tree is re-clonable by
# scripts/fetch-torque3d.sh and its contents are not expected to survive;
# scripts/link-game-files.cmd junctions it back to the data/ directory the
# engine resolves against its own executable.
assets/
game-files/*
!game-files/README.md

# Extracted levels, if a level zip is ever unpacked inside the tree.
content/

# BeamNG's own formats, and the artefacts of converting them. None of these
# appear in the repository legitimately, so they are ignored wherever they
# land — including outside the directories above.
*.ter
*.terrain.json
*.materials.json
*.forestbrushes.json
*.cdae
*.tsmesh
*.prefab
*.jbeam
*.pc
items.level.json

# Local agent state. Not part of the project.
.workbuddy-ai/

# Third-party source checkouts. Fetched by scripts/fetch-torque3d.sh, not
# vendored — the tree is ~900 MB. The pin file IS tracked: it records which
# upstream commit the build expects.
third_party/*
!third_party/Torque3D.pin

# Build output
build/
out/
*.o
*.obj
*.a
*.lib
*.exe
*.wasm
*.wasm.map

# Test output. The TORQUE_TESTING build writes gtest XML to the working
# directory, which for scripts/build-native.cmd is the repository root.
test_detail.xml

# Browser test harness. node_modules is restored by `npm install`; the
# Playwright output directories are written on every run.
node_modules/
test-results/
playwright-report/

# Emscripten
.emscripten_cache/

# Editor / OS
.vs/
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Logs
*.log
